& [ProviderNeutralSchema] is closed
  + [tool_name] is cantor.exchange
  + [schema_version] is cantor.exchange/0.1
  + [protocol_operations] are propose, challenge, qualify, cite, reconcile, poll, acknowledge, yield, and stop
  + [first_executable_operation] is reconcile only
  + named but unimplemented operations fail with operation_not_executable rather than inheriting behavior
  + exact required input and output field names, closed inputs, closed outputs, effect class, checkpoint contract, identity, and digest are machine visible
  + the schema contains no provider-specific request, response, token, hidden-state, or transport form

& [CheckpointController] is deterministic and effectless
  + one supplied structured proposal pins schema, call, inference job, participant, pass, invocation, session, and argument digest
  + the controller records generation_opened, tool_call_proposed, and generation_stopped before validation or Cantor invocation
  + accepted calls record tool_call_validated, Cantor_invoked, tool_result_returned, context_bound, later_pass_resumed, and completed in that exact order
  + refused calls record call_refused and completed without Cantor invocation evidence, explicit context, or later-pass resume
  + logical time is derived from the invocation input and event index rather than a physical clock
  + every transcript event binds its predecessor, payload digest, logical time, call, index, identity, and event digest

& [EvidenceAndContextBoundary] is exact
  + supplied authorship lane evidence is independently replayed before the call can cross the boundary
  + exact admitted invocation and negotiation session lineage are required
  + the accepted call reruns the catalogue coordination rather than trusting a supplied outcome
  + the structured result binds invocation-result digest, explicit output projection, admission, replay, and semantic-trace proof references
  + LaterPassContext names the next pass and contains only an inspectable value plus result digest and sensitivity
  + context is input to a later inference pass and never represented as mutation of an uninterrupted decode pass

& [VerificationBoundary] is independent
  + transcript verification checks schema identity, zero provider and external effects, result binding, causal event chain, exact accepted or refused stage sequence, outcome shape, context pass progression, and content digests
  + changed arguments, unsupported operations, substituted evidence, reordered events, changed results, unknown fields, and unknown operations fail visibly
  + deterministic replay produces byte-equivalent schema, result, coordination, and transcript values

& [EffectBoundary] is unchanged
  + provider_call_count is zero
  + external_effect_count is zero
  + no model, llama.cpp server, provider API, tokenizer, hidden activation, K/V cache, persistence, filesystem runtime, network, system clock, process, thread, notification, Git operation, unsafe code, hardware, or FPGA path is invoked by the implementation

& [SolutionDisposition] is accepted for CPPE-I08 after completed-work review
